title: Maintain a wiki
tags: Contents

A project that keeps its documentation on DecentraWiki, Bisq's wiki say, works like this.

!!! Publish the wiki under the project's name

Publish the first version and point the project's ENS name, or a subname such as `wiki.yourproject.eth`, at the wiki's address, `ipns://k51…`, once. See [[Give a wiki a name]]. Readers who open the name get the newest version.

!!! Take in the versions readers publish

Anyone may publish an edited version, and each one gets its own address. Nothing reaches the project's name until a maintainer points it there. When a reader sends you the address of a version:

# In the editor, press ''Import'' and paste the version's address, `ipfs://bafy…`.
# The editor fetches it from public IPFS gateways, checking every block against the address, and sees that it is a version of a wiki you already have. It says how many tiddlers changed, were added or were removed, and names them.
# Choose ''Add as a new wiki'' to read it beside your own copy, or ''Replace my copy'' to take it whole.
# Publish the result and choose ''Update its address''. The project's name shows it, with no new transaction.

The versions a project did not take stay at their own IPFS addresses, readable by anyone who has them.

!!! Several maintainers

Each maintainer edits in their own browser. Whoever holds the key of the wiki's address decides which version it shows: keep the key file safe, and share it only with the maintainers who may publish. A maintainer imports it in the editor (''Settings'', ''Addresses'', ''Import a key''). The name's owner, a person or a multisig wallet, points the ENS name at the wiki's address once.